# 11. Adding Multiple Elements Using extend()

`extend()` adds multiple elements from another iterable to the end of a list.

```python
fruits = ["Apple", "Banana"]

more_fruits = ["Orange", "Mango"]

fruits.extend(more_fruits)

print(fruits)
```

Output:

```text
['Apple', 'Banana', 'Orange', 'Mango']
```

### Real-World Example

Combining two shopping lists:

```python
shopping_list1 = ["Milk", "Bread"]
shopping_list2 = ["Eggs", "Rice"]

shopping_list1.extend(shopping_list2)

print(shopping_list1)
```

