# 52. sort() vs sorted()

`sort()` changes the original list.

```python
numbers = [30, 10, 20]

numbers.sort()

print(numbers)
```

`sorted()` creates and returns a new sorted list.

```python
numbers = [30, 10, 20]

new_numbers = sorted(numbers)

print(numbers)
print(new_numbers)
```

Output:

```text
[30, 10, 20]
[10, 20, 30]
```

